<title>USA: Lebanon offers $100 mln 10-year yankee bond.</title>
<headline>Lebanon offers $100 mln 10-year yankee bond.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lebanese Republic is offering $100 million bonds due 2007 to qualified institutional investors under Rule 144 A of the U.S. Securities Act, according to a prelimary prospectus.</p>
<p>The bonds are guranteed by the World Bank only as to the payment of principal at maturity, it said.</p>
<p>Merill Lynch International is the lead manager.</p>
<p>(( -- Emerging Markets Desk - 212-859-1674))</p>
</text>
